{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:60ae363002bbdc3c","name":"Brute","source":{"id":"source:reference-60ae363002bbdc3c","title":"Brute","revision":25833,"timestamp":"2024-12-24T11:43:15Z","sha256":"127bd55ce278aff38c9feeba2ed472745e8102a158fe9801e2b1cdbf110c8c4b","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25833","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Brute&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-60ae363002bbdc3c","blocks":[{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["Brute Units\n"],"colspan":2}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Brute Squad"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Brute_Squad","referenceId":"reference:e6a91adbf773d00c"},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["\n"]},"\n"],"colspan":2}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Brute Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Brute_Battalion","referenceId":"reference:45e3614061ae9d66"},"\n"],"colspan":2}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Brutes are ubiquitous members of galactic society and can be found anywhere, even on the most peaceful of planets. Brutes are typically crude and unsubtle, regardless of whether they work for some ",{"tag":"a","children":["Crime Lord"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Crime_Lord","referenceId":"reference:6f4563ed64c9640b"}," or act independently. Most are motivated by a simple agenda- greed, power, fear of superiors, or even, on occasion, loyalty. They are rarely well armed or armored, making do with whatever they can find, although they constantly look to find something better (or rob someone who has superior ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"},"). Brutes strive to gain more status and wealth and will do almost anything to get it, up to and including murder. In turn, Brutes typically despise authority figures, especially ",{"tag":"a","children":["Police Officers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Police_Officers"},", military figures, and Jedi. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Brute presented here could be a gun-toting gang member or an organized crime soldier. Alternatively, the statistics could also represent a militia member or a raw conscript who has little training (in which case, remove the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side Score"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Side_Score"},").\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Brute Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["By their very nature, Brutes can be found almost anywhere. They serve as nameless antagonists in every situation- from the high streets of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"}," to the lowly slums of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tatooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tatooine","referenceId":"reference:a1b911e88e4876e1"},". Brutes commonly travel in pairs or larger groups, each group representing a street gang, a crime syndicate hit squad, or a tribe of warriors. By their very nature, Brutes typically respond to threats or opposition with muscle and violence, but they can be swayed by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intimidation"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intimidation"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persuasion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persuasion","referenceId":"reference:196fbdc5f1823320"},", or bribes. However, not all Brutes are antagonistic- they can also be used as nameless allies and warriors on the side of the heroes. The Brute works fine as a generic spearholder, cannon fodder to be used in the background, or an ordinary (if tough) nonplayer character for the GM to use throughout adventures.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Encounters involving Brutes typically occur at lower levels, where they are a threat to the heroes. When the heroes have advanced to 6th level or beyond, the number of Brutes required to make a credible threat runs over a dozen, making them difficult to coordinate in combat. Thus, individual Brutes should be scaled up to represent stronger threats, or another archetype should be chosen. Alternatively, a group of Brutes could be paired up with much more powerful leaders (often with Heroic Levels) or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," equipped with serious firepower.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Brute Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side Score"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Side_Score"},":"]}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +7; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +0\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 11 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 10), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 11, ",{"tag":"a","chi